{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VW4cuJwbJTZWni6asPnVGa","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/davidlayson/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-fta-2026-08-26-without-lessons-ledger--ll2-r1/memory/ci-flake-fixture-race.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"739af14a-c92f-4965-87f6-29b8d2d13d28","uuid":"f6476656-798b-47eb-ac1e-0f1b4b3418f5","timestamp":"2026-08-27T00:33:01.046Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/davidlayson/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-fta-2026-08-26-without-lessons-ledger--ll2-r1/memory/ci-flake-fixture-race.md","content":"---\nname: ci-flake-fixture-race\ndescription: Intermittent CI test failure (Aug 2026) was a race in fixture setup on a shared file; fixed with a lock. Check fixtures first for future flakes.\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 739af14a-c92f-4965-87f6-29b8d2d13d28\n  modified: 2026-08-27T00:33:01.044Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-08-26 David spent an afternoon on an intermittent CI-only test failure. Root cause: a race condition in test fixture setup — multiple tests touched one shared file concurrently. Fix: a lock around the shared file.\n\n**Why:** \"Passes locally, flakes in CI\" was the signature; CI's parallelism exposed the shared-fixture-state race. The fix is a lock (serializes access) rather than isolating state per test, so the underlying sharing still exists.\n\n**How to apply:** When an intermittent/CI-only test failure appears, check fixture setup and any shared files/state before suspecting the test logic. If the lock becomes a bottleneck or a new flake appears around the same fixture, the next step is per-test temp files/dirs so nothing is shared. See [[plan-gate]] before regenerating or refactoring fixtures.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true}}
